# castoff Wi-Fi credentials -- edit this file BEFORE the Pi's first boot.
#
# This appliance has no keyboard, mouse or monitor attached once deployed, so
# this file is the only way to get it onto your Wi-Fi network. After flashing
# the SD card image (see README's "Raspberry Pi 4 image" section):
#
#   1. Re-mount the SD card's root filesystem -- the larger, second (ext4)
#      partition, NOT the small "FIRMWARE" FAT partition -- on a Linux
#      machine (or WSL).
#   2. Edit /etc/castoff/wifi-credentials.env there (this file, at that path
#      in the image) and replace the two placeholder values below with your
#      real network name and password.
#   3. Unmount, insert the card into the Pi, and power it on.
#
# Format: plain KEY=value lines, no quotes, no spaces around `=`, one per
# line. Skipping this step leaves the device with no Wi-Fi connection
# (Ethernet still works if plugged in) -- NetworkManager just fails to
# associate with these placeholder values and the appliance boots normally
# otherwise; nothing about first boot depends on this file being edited.
WIFI_SSID=YourNetworkName
WIFI_PSK=YourNetworkPassword
